															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/logarithmika" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1884068); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1884068&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834355" alt="Logarithmika" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1884068)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/logarithmika" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1884068); return false;" >Logarithmika</a></span> <span class="odate time_1579384764 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Jan 2020 21:59</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4472709">
									

<p>First, thank you all for taking the time to read this entry for the 5000 contest. Quite nervous, too, since it's been more than a year since <a href="/scp-4079">my last attempt</a> at writing an SCP. I'd be thankful for any feedback and constructive criticism so I can improve this piece. Even if it doesn't fly, it will be helpful so I can learn from the mistakes I made here in my future attempts at contributing to the site. (I just hope that, if this burns down, I'll get to read the feedback before this hits -10&#8230;)</p>
<p>I would like to thank <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/oricat" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5199638); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5199638&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579385675" alt="OriCat" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5199638)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/oricat" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5199638); return false;">OriCat</a></span> for taking the time to read and comment on two quite different versions of this, and even researching for some useful resources. Their feedback was extremely helpful, even if some of it wasn't implemented due to time and real life constraints. Thanks!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers&nbsp;to&nbsp;get&nbsp;what&nbsp;is&nbsp;going&nbsp;on&nbsp;(do&nbsp;not&nbsp;read&nbsp;if&nbsp;you&nbsp;haven't&nbsp;read&nbsp;SCP-4028&nbsp;first!)</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>Pierre Menard is fictional <strong>in-universe</strong> (as well as a good chunk of the Pataphysics Department itself— probably not everyone, as <em>somebody</em> has to write the SCP files and etc., but who knows). With that in mind, please re-read the last part of the exploration log.</li>
<li>I'm using <span style="color: blue">blue text</span> in the same fashion as in several other articles on this wiki: to indicate a revision or edit. The implication is that everything that involves Menard in the expedition log is made up, to accomplish the mentioned &quot;narrative containment procedures&quot;.</li>
<li>There is a hidden collapsible at the bottom, just below the last bit of blue text.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Commentary&nbsp;about&nbsp;inspiration&nbsp;(do&nbsp;not&nbsp;read&nbsp;if&nbsp;you&nbsp;haven't&nbsp;opened&nbsp;the&nbsp;previous&nbsp;collapsible)</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This was partially inspired by some post (either here or in Reddit) that commented on the possibility of the SK being functionally contained by <a href="/scp-2747">SCP-2747</a>. Sadly, I lost the link and I don't remember enough of the post to be able to Google it properly, so if by any chance the author of that post happens to read this, I'd be happy to credit them as the original inspiration.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Image&nbsp;attributions</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The third image (Penrose tiling) is sourced from <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roger-Penrose-Kachelstruktur.jpg">here</a>. It is licensed under CC-BY-SA 2.5, which I <em>think</em> is forward-compatible with 4.0, but I am not sure. Please tell me if it has to be removed, so I can find/draw/render a suitable replacement.<br />
The second image (constellation) is from <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Cygnus_X#/media/File:Young_Stellar_Grouping_in_Cygnus_X_(6426254159).jpg">here</a>, and it is public domain.<br />
The first image (flower and thorns) is drawn by me, and I license it under CC-BY-SA 4.0, etc.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thanks, and hopefully this is enjoyable for you all!</p>
<p>EDIT: With the nerves I forgot to add the desired slots for after the contest. (Thanks, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quicksilvers" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3485737); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3485737&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579385675" alt="Quicksilvers" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3485737)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quicksilvers" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3485737); return false;">Quicksilvers</a></span>!) I think that, in descending order, I'd apply for: 5317, 5079, 5777, 5670 and 5772)</p>

							</div>

								
