<p>I enjoy the concept of this skip and think it's well-executed, but I do have some nitpicks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The floor is composed of marble, and the room has an architectural style similar in appearance to a Catholic cathedral, with wooden iconography associated to Christianity, Islam and Judaism present along the floor and walls.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Christianity, Judaism, and Islam aren't really all that similar. They have a common origin, yes, but so do golden moles and blue whales. There should be a good reason to group them together, one that I didn't spot.</p>
<p>The dialogue used a lot of &quot;it is&quot;, &quot;I am&quot;, etc. statements, which felt a little awkward. People usually say &quot; it's&quot;, &quot;I'm&quot;, etc.</p>
<p>There were a lot of crosslinks. I'd recommend trimming them down to only the important ones - I just ended up not reading any of them because it would've taken far too long.</p>
<p>Otherwise, the concept of a narrative, self-containing SCP is fantastic, and I thought you did the idea justice! +1</p>

