			<div class="content" id="post-content-4522774">
									

<p>Thank you for your kind comment. ^^</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Response&nbsp;to&nbsp;commentary</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>You are the second person who mentions an excessive number of crosslinks, so I decided to remove the most egregious ones. The reasoning for them was twofold: first, I'm the kind of person who likes to wiki-walk, and I usually open the links in separate tabs to read them later. I forgot to consider that not everyone does the same, whoops. The second reason is tied with the name of the SCP (&quot;Misdirection&quot;)&#8212; the idea, out of universe, was for people to speculate about the true nature of the tower by offering several false leads. (Note that a certain spoilery GoI is not mentioned at all in the main text and only appears explicitly in the hidden collapsible).</p>
<p>To note, the removed crosslinks are: <a href="/scp-2935">SCP-2935</a> (whose purpose was explicitly to be a red herring), <a href="/numbers-never-die">Numbers, Like Stories, Never Die</a> (I wanted to leave it ambiguous whether the D-11424 here is the original one or the girl from that tale, hence the use of neutral pronouns through the text and the crosslink, but again, not thematically related), the one to the Rat's Nest hub (again, red herring, although it was also clarifying Dr. Lockhart's statement) and the link to <a href="/spikebrennan-s-proposal">Spikebrennan's Proposal</a> (which I should admit was there mostly as a really bad pun). Maybe I should remove the crosslink to <a href="/scp-3882">SCP-3882</a> as well, but since that phrase from Lockhart explicitly references the events there, I've decided to keep that one for now.</p>
<p>Each floor we get to see is dedicated to a specific GoI. The reason for Islam to be grouped together with Christianity and Judaism is that the corresponding floor is dedicated to the Horizon Initiative.</p>
<p>I suppose I'm too used to avoid contractions when writing academic-esque texts and that slipped to the video transcript, which isn't an academic text at all. I've tried to make it somewhat better, thanks for pointing it out. <span style="font-size:50%;">(I had the opposite problem with an early version of a paper I was working on&#8212; contractions kept slipping in&#8230;)</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I'm glad that this seems to work for most of the people who have commented here. Once again, thank you for the criticism as well&#8212; if there is something else that can be done to improve this, I'll be glad to read about it.</p>

